# Unhashed assets change in place between deploys, so they must be revalidated
# instead of sitting in a browser (or edge) cache. Without this, a fresh deploy
# can pair new HTML with a stale stylesheet, and the page renders with the old
# layout - e.g. the product page's launch button dropping out of the header
# because site.css had no .prod-head rules yet. (The app's Vite bundles under
# /products/<product>/app/assets/ are content-hashed, so they keep long caching.)
#
# NOTE: on the manumit.studio custom domain the zone's browser cache currently
# overrides these to max-age=14400 (the pages.dev deployment honors them), so
# `npm run assemble` additionally stamps ?v=<content hash> on shell CSS/JS
# references - changed bytes always mean a new URL, so a deploy can never pair
# new HTML with a stale asset. Set the zone's Caching > Browser Cache TTL to
# "Respect Origin Headers" to make this file authoritative there too.
#
# Security boundary: /api/* is served by the Worker, which already answers
# `Cache-Control: no-store` on every JSON response. These static rules never
# touch per-user data - the pull stays fresh via client `cache: 'no-store'` +
# `_ts` buster and the server `version` conditional (`{ unchanged: true }`).
/site.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/policies/policies.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/nav.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

